course: dictionary
lesson: 7232
title: What is physics?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Physics is the science of matter and energy and how they act. It looks at forces, motion, light, sound, heat, electricity, magnetism and the universe. When you see a new science word, look at the words around it, because they are its context.
explain: «Gravity pulls at once when there is no ground below; the coyote's pause in the air is «cartoon physics», put there so the audience has time to laugh.» The phrase «cartoon physics» means pretend physics. In real physics the coyote would fall at once, so the cartoon bends the rules for fun.
explain: In school, physics lessons often cover forces like gravity and friction, circuits, shadows, magnets, and space. People who work in this science are physicists, and a «physics teacher» is the person who teaches it. Phrases like «laws of physics» mean the rules that nature always follows.
fact: Physics is one of the main sciences, along with chemistry and biology.
fact: Physics studies forces such as gravity and friction, and how things move.
fact: CERN, «a big European physics lab in Switzerland», is a place where scientists study matter and energy.
fact: «Cartoon physics» means cartoon rules that break the real laws of physics for fun.
fact: Albert Einstein was very good at physics and maths as a boy, so the idea that he failed maths is a myth.
exercise: What does physics study? | *Forces, motion, light, sound and energy | Only old stories and poems | Only plants and animals | Only numbers in a bank
exercise: In the sentence «CERN, a big European physics lab in Switzerland», what is CERN? | *A big physics lab in Switzerland | A city in Italy | A football club | A type of cake
exercise: From the sentence «he did well in maths and physics but not in other subjects», which subjects did Einstein do well in? | Every subject | *Maths and physics | Only English | Art and music
test: Which of these is a force that physics studies? | *Gravity | Bread | Cloud | Sandwich
test: Complete the phrase: the ___ of physics are the rules nature always follows. | *Laws | Wings | Colours | Recipes
exam: Which best describes physics? | *Science of matter and energy, forces, light, sound and heat | Study of the names of countries | Study of old stories and poems | Art of drawing cartoons
